# =============================================================================
# JuniperData Docker Build Exclusions
# =============================================================================
# Excludes files not needed in the Docker build context to reduce image size
# and build time. Keep in sync with .gitignore where applicable.
# =============================================================================

# Git and version control
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# IDE and editor files
.vscode/
.idea/
.trunk/
*.swp
*.swo

# Python artifacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*.pyd
.Python
*.egg-info/
# ``*.egg-info/`` matches only the context root. juniper-data is not vulnerable
# to the build-provenance version-shadow today (it runs ``python -m juniper_data``
# off the installed package, and its egg-info is at the repo root) — these nested
# forms are defense-in-depth + ecosystem consistency with the canopy #362 / cascor
# fixes (a stale ``*/foo.egg-info`` COPYed onto an import path can shadow the
# installed package version).
**/*.egg-info/
**/*.dist-info/
*.egg
dist/
build/
wheels/
*.whl

# Test and coverage
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
.coverage
**/.coverage
htmlcov/
**/htmlcov/
reports/
*.prof
TEST*.xml
TEST*.html

# Development tools
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.serena/
.claude/

# Documentation (not needed at runtime)
docs/
notes/
*.md
!README.md

# Local data and logs (will be mounted as volumes)
data/
logs/
images/

# Configuration files not needed in container
conf/
util/
src/

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.temp
*.log
**/*.log
*.out

# Large media files
*.mp4
*.avi
*.mov
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.png
*.xcf

# Archives
*.gz
*.tgz
*.tar
*.zip
*.bz

# Test suite and its artifacts.
#
# `COPY juniper_data/ ./juniper_data/` (Dockerfile:30) is DIRECTORY-grained, not
# file-grained, so without these rules the published image carries the suite.
# Measured 2026-09-21 INSIDE the pulled artifact, not inferred:
# `juniper-data:0.14.0` shipped **87** files named `test_*.py` -- 95 `.py` files and 190
# files in total under `tests/`, `tests/fixtures/` included. (#405 said 22; recounted in
# the pulled image 2026-09-21 and no criterion reproduces it -- top-level is 3, and the
# per-subdir test_*.py split is unit 75 / integration 9 / performance 2 / api 1. The rule
# #405 added is correct and unchanged; only the figure moved.)
#
# The `**/` prefix is load-bearing, and the existing `reports/` and `htmlcov/`
# entries above show why: a bare pattern matches the CONTEXT ROOT only, so
# `reports/` never protected `juniper_data/tests/reports/`. The suite lives at
# `juniper_data/tests/`, one level down.
#
# This is also a credential guard. A CI publish builds from a CLEAN CHECKOUT, so
# only COMMITTED files can reach an image -- which is what keeps the juniper-deploy
# `secrets/` class (eight live credential files in a working tree with no
# `.dockerignore`) from reproducing here. But a credential COMMITTED anywhere under
# `juniper_data/tests/` would ship into a published production image, and no
# Docker-level control would stop it.
#
# Nothing depends on the tests being present in the image.
**/tests/
**/reports/

# -- Credentials. Docker does NOT honour .gitignore, and this image is PUBLIC.
#    The Dockerfile copies a DIRECTORY allowlist, which is not a file allowlist:
#    `COPY <pkg>/ ./<pkg>/` ships everything tracked beneath it. Patterns are
#    root-anchored (Go filepath.Match), so the `**/` twins are load-bearing.
secrets/
**/secrets/
*.key
**/*.key
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
